 \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The stream name cant contain arbitrary symbols as documented\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"source_a.md documents this constraint for Java agents; source_b.md documents it for browser agents.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-003\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Stream names are validated against ^[A-Za-z0-9 -]+$ before the agent registers.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"source_a.md directly states this claim verbatim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-004\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Put plainly: letters, digits, spaces and hyphens only, and nothing else, or the agent refuses to start.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"source_a.md directly states that stream names contain only these character types.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-005\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"or the agent refuses to start.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"source_a.md states the agent refuses to start if unsupported characters are used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-006\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The Nimbrel Probe stream name is what seperates one instrumented process from the next.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"source_b.md directly states this claim with a minor spelling variation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-007\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Stream name containing a . (dot) for exampe` checkout.web` along with a number of other symbols are refused by Nimbrel Probe\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"source_b.md explicitly states that dots are refused in stream names.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-008\",\n 